From 11151dda15665812369b615318dff7fa989c3e37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 04:37:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] frontend: Add scene tree layout model

Scene folders need a data model that is independent from the Qt
widget, so that loading, saving and undo/redo can share one tested
implementation.

The layout of the Scenes dock is described as a list of top-level
entries (scenes and folders with their scenes). It is persisted in a
way that stays compatible with versions of OBS without folders:

* "scene_order" keeps the flat list of all scenes in display order, so
  older versions still load every scene in the same order.
* Folder membership is stored in each scene's private settings
  ("scene_folder"), which every version of OBS preserves.
* The folder list (name, collapsed state, position) is stored in a new
  top-level "scene_folders" array that older versions ignore.

When "scene_folders" is missing (e.g. the collection was saved by an
older version), folders are rebuilt from the private settings at the
position of their first scene.

Also adds a cmocka test for the save/load round trip and the
compatibility cases.
