From 5ae89536c2107325fa0759031065361e963f6fab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 04:40:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] frontend: Add folders to the Scenes dock

Large scene collections are hard to navigate, especially when many
scenes only exist to be nested into other scenes. This adds collapsible
folders to the Scenes dock, which are purely organizational: folders are
not sources, have no hotkeys, and scene enumeration (multiview,
obs_frontend_get_scenes, scene switching) keeps returning all scenes in
the order of the dock.

The SceneTree stays a QListWidget, so grid mode and existing code that
walks the rows keep working. Folder headers are additional rows, and
scenes directly following a folder header that are flagged as being in
a folder belong to it. Folders cannot be nested.

* Folders can be added, renamed (F2/inline editor) and removed from the
  context menu. Removing a folder keeps its scenes at the same position.
* Folders are expanded/collapsed with their indicator (the same theme
  indicator the Sources dock uses for groups), by double-clicking them,
  or with the Left/Right keys. Collapsed folders hide their scenes in
  both list and grid mode.
* Scenes are moved into and out of folders by drag and drop (drop onto
  a folder, between its scenes, or below/above it) or with the new
  "Move to Folder" context menu, which can also create a folder.
* Move Up/Down/Top/Bottom move scenes within their folder, and move
  folders together with their scenes.
* A scene that becomes current while its folder is collapsed (hotkey,
  studio mode, API) reveals it by expanding the folder.
* "Show Folder Scenes in Multiview" toggles all scenes of a folder.
* All folder edits and scene reordering by drag and drop can be undone.
  Undoing the removal of a scene restores it into its folder.
* Folder rows expose their state through accessibility descriptions.

The layout is saved with the model added in the previous commit, so
collections stay loadable by older versions of OBS and keep their folders
when they are saved by an older version.
